name: Mobile financial services fraud
tagline: "A seeded mobile financial services fraud Link Analysis demo - SIM-swap wallet takeover, agent split deposits and merchant cash-out collusion, planted among 8 000 wallets, 300 agents and 400 merchants with benign look-alikes"
description: "The mobile financial services (MFS) fraud Link Analysis demo as a Space Template, Basic tier. Seven synthetic feeds (agent, merchant, wallet, wallet_txn, sim_event, device_login, agent_commission; 12 months landed from 2025-10-01 in data/inbox, the next month in data/staged; 7 900 wallets, 300 agents, 400 merchants, about 101 000 wallet transactions, 1 150 SIM events and 69 000 wallet-handset-days) are landed by seven Collectors and Pipelines. The mfs_links Job folds them into ONE link Dataset (src, dst, kind, ts, amount, event_date, via) of seven link kinds; the mfs_screen_links Job derives the three fraud screens the saved views read. Planted stories (ground truth: tools/gen-la-mfs-data.ground-truth.json; pinned by MfsLinksJobGoldenTest and tools/gen-la-mfs-data.test.mjs): one call-centre login swaps 30 customers' SIMs in 10 days and each wallet is drained within 2 hours to 5 mule wallets that cash out at 2 agents; an agent splits the deposits of 120 wallets it registered itself into many small cash-ins to earn a commission on each; a merchant opened 3 weeks ago is paid by 60 new wallets minutes after each was funded at one of 3 agents and settles every day. Benign look-alikes that must not join a story: a busy store running a SIM upgrade drive, a market agent whose traders make many small deposits, and a popular grocery whose shoppers often pay right after a cash-in. Wallet anti-money-laundering (structuring, mule chains, a device farm) is in la-mobile-money. Three saved views. Basic tier: runs on every edition, Basic included. Advanced tier, in the same template and inert on Basic: Demo Users and roles (config/demo-users.toon, roles.toon: mfs.analyst lead, mfs.manager second approver, mfs.reviewer read-only, mfs.outsider not a member, admin), four-eyes above a fan-out of 2000 and Drafts (link-analysis.toon), the mfs_swap_drain_counts and mfs_swap_drain_alerts Jobs and the Alert Rule mfs_wallet_drained_after_sim_swap (on the shipped data it counts 30 wallets that paid out 300 or more within 2 hours of a SIM swap, all swapped by one login, S-41; no other wallet paid out more than 98.14 within 2 hours of a swap, so the store's SIM upgrade drive is never counted; unarmed on Basic). Investigations, members, an Entity List, a Case, a held four-eyes expand and a Draft are runtime state: run `node tools/seed-la-mfs.mjs --apply` on an Advanced or Preview build with Demo Auth. Synthetic data only."
minEdition: basic
icon: heroicons_outline:device-phone-mobile
contents[7]: "7 Collectors + Pipelines + Datasets (12 months landed, 1 month staged)", "mfs_links Job + Dataset (7 link kinds, via) and the mfs_screen_links Dataset of three fraud screens", "3 saved views (SIM swap bursts, split deposits, merchant quick pay)", "3 planted stories with benign look-alikes", "Ground truth and golden tests in the repository", "Advanced tier: 5 Demo Users + role table, four-eyes (inert on Basic)", "Advanced tier: Alert Rule on a wallet drained within 2 hours of a SIM swap (counts Job + evaluate Job, unarmed on Basic)"
